  (text "FROM THE HAND-WRITTEN NETLIST THIS SHEET REPLACES (verbatim; the part notes are on each part's Note field):\n\nA LONE NO-CONNECT PIN'S NET IS NAMED AFTER THE PIN (the export names it so, whatever label it carries), so the\none-pin nets the text below names are, on this sheet: DAC_CH6_UNUSED is VOUTF; DAC_CH8_UNUSED is VOUTH.\n\nAUTHORITATIVE for connectivity. The ASCII drawing in dac8568.md is a REPRESENTATION of this file.\n\nTHE DRAWING SHOWS TWO PINS OF SIXTEEN. It was split out of digital-and-supervision.md to carry the CLR and\nLDAC corrections, and those are all it draws - the SPI pins, the rail, the ground and all six live outputs are\nprose in the ## Interfaces table and nowhere in the picture. They are netted here. That gap is the reason a\nnetlist is worth more than a redraw: a picture of two pins cannot be wrong about the other fourteen, and it\ncannot be right about them either.\n\nPin names are SBAS430E's own, from the 16-pin TSSOP PIN DESCRIPTIONS table of the banked\ndatasheets/analog/DAC8568CIPW.pdf [datasheet]: 1 LDAC   2 SYNC   3 AVDD   4 VOUTA  5 VOUTC  6 VOUTE  7 VOUTG 8\nVREFIN/VREFOUT  9 CLR   10 VOUTH 11 VOUTF 12 VOUTD 13 VOUTB 14 GND  15 DIN   16 SCLK\n\n[pins] CHANNEL NUMBER TO DATASHEET LETTER IS ORDINAL HERE: ch1=VOUTA through ch8=VOUTH, so the two spares are\nVOUTF and VOUTH. NO DOCUMENT IN THIS CORPUS STATES THAT MAP [derived, not cited] - ADR 0006 allocates by\nnumber and the datasheet names by letter, and nothing joins them. It is the only reading consistent with\n\"channels 6 and 8 spare\", and it decides which two pins a layout leaves unconnected, so it is asserted here\nrather than left implied. Contradict it in ADR 0006 if it is wrong and this file follows.\n\n[LDAC] LOCAL, and it crosses no boundary: the pin and its strap, nothing else. That is the whole content of\nthe LDAC correction.\n\n[VOUTF] THE TWO SPARES, NAMED SO THEY ARE NO-CONNECT BY DECISION RATHER THAN BY OMISSION. An unlisted pin and\na pin listed as going nowhere read the same in a picture and not at all the same in a layout review.\n\nNets with one endpoint on purpose." (at 256.54 38.099999999999994 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid b9ffbaf9-0630-5b2b-9542-44087951313b))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
)
